e": "Triangle closures inside the group (notably 169-331-369 around 19.0k-20.6k and 12-304-1058 around 20.6k-22.2k) occur with successive edges under 800 time units apart, giving a closure wave ending near t\u224822.2k. A time-respecting, \u2264600-gap route 667\u2192734\u2192449\u21921188\u2192731 runs from \u224825.1k to \u224825.9k, starting ~2.9k units after the wave ends, i.e. inside the 4000-unit admissible period. Low degrees of 667 and 731 and the modest overall event volume rule out popularity/volume explanations; the path is temporally ordered, not merely static."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Part 1 \u2014 Closure wave in the group.**\nThe group is sparse (3\u20136 partners each, step_02) yet every one of the 12 nodes sits in exactly one static triangle (step_04, 12 incident triangles). Two triangles are internal/near-internal and I could time them:\n\n- **{169, 331, 369}** (step_12, 16, 17): their events fall in consecutive ~400-unit bins at \u224819.0k, 19.8k, 20.2k, 20.6k (step_31) \u2014 successive edges of the triad established within <800 units of each other, i.e. a genuine closure.\n- **{12, 304, 1058}** (step_08, 14, 32): events at \u224820.6k, 21.4k, 21.8k, 22.2k (step_21, 30) \u2014 again gaps well under 800, closing the triad. The **last closing interaction lands \u224822.2k**.\n\nSo the wave runs roughly 18.9k \u2192 ~22.2k.\n\n**Part 2 \u2014 Temporal route 667 \u2192 731.**\n667 has only 2 events in the whole window (step_03), so the route is not an artefact of node popularity. The static 2-hop neighbourhood of 667 (step_05) and the 3-hop neighbourhood of 731 (step_07) intersect on the chain 667 \u2192 734 \u2192 449 \u2192 1188 \u2192 731; all four edges exist and are directed the right way inside [24401, 27400] (steps 23\u201326). Timing them finely (steps 27\u201329): 667\u2192734 \u224825.1k, 734\u2192449 \u224825.3k, 449\u21921188 \u224825.7k, 1188\u2192731 \u224825.9k (731's single event falls in 25801\u201326000, step_28). Every inter-step gap is \u2264600, and the steps are strictly increasing.\n\n**Coupling.** Route start \u224825.1k minus wave end \u224822.2k \u2248 2.9k < 4000 \u2014 the route begins inside the admissible post-wave period. The connection is not merely static (step_05/07 show the static path, but steps 27\u201329 show it is also time-respecting), and 667/731 are low-degree, ruling out a volume/popularity explanation.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d75c93b0\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"compound\",\n  \"entities\": [12, 17, 34, 64, 169, 209, 304, 323, 331, 369, 401, 599, 667, 731, 734, 449, 1188],\n  \"window\": [18400, 36065],\n  \"confidence\": 0.68,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Triangle closures inside the group (notably 169-331-369 around 19.0k-20.6k and 12-304-1058 around 20.6k-22.2k) occur with successive edges under 800 time units apart, giving a closure wave ending near t\u224822.2k. A time-respecting, \u2264600-gap route 667\u2192734\u2192449\u21921188\u2192731 runs from \u224825.1k to \u224825.9k, starting ~2.9k units after the wave ends, i.e. inside the 4000-unit admissible period. Low degrees of 667 and 731 and the modest overall event volume rule out popularity/volume explanations; the path is temporally ordered, not merely static.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 83531, "total_output_tokens": 14446, "total_tokens": 97977, "total_latency_ms": 204156, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}